{
    "test_name": "MOB.805_Search_Filter_Edit",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.805_Search_Filter_Edit",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.805` **Editing an existing `StructuredQuery` filter** \u2014 the branch `MOB.800` never\nreaches.\n- `MOB.800` builds a filter and clears it. **Nothing had ever edited one**, and edit is a\n  separate path: clicking an active pill sets `editFilterIndex`, a `useEffect` rebinds the\n  draft form, `Add Filter` becomes **`Update Filter`**, `Cancel edit` appears, and\n  submitting **replaces** `filters[i]` instead of appending.\n- **StructuredQuery builds server-side conditions**, so a defect returns *wrong data*\n  rather than a visibly broken control \u2014 the reason its second branch is worth covering.\n- \u2b50 **It asserts the form contents, not just the button text.** A label flip only proves\n  `editFilterIndex` moved; the round trip (`#value` absent after Add \u2192 `Pump 0102` after\n  clicking the pill) is what proves the draft rebound to the **right** filter.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **Every filter renders as TWO pills** \u2014 `ActiveFilters` inside the drawer and\n  `FilterInfo` in the always-visible bar outside it, both wired to `onSelect`. A\n  page-level pill locator matches both (trap 3), so everything here is scoped to the\n  **drawer's** copy.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **Clicks the pill's LABEL, never the pill's remove button.** `Pill withRemoveButton`\n  carries both handlers millimetres apart; hitting the wrong one deletes the filter and\n  fails a later assertion for a reason that looks nothing like the cause.\n- \ud83d\uded1 **Asserts that Cancel PRESERVES the filter** \u2014 `cancelEdit` touches only the draft, and\n  a cancel that quietly dropped the filter would otherwise read as a clean pass.\n- **READ-ONLY** against the server: filters are client-side query state, held in an\n  **in-memory** store (`utils.ts:38` \u2014 not localStorage), so a `goToUrl` clears them. The\n  test still clears its own filter with `alwaysExecute`.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Search",
            "StructuredQuery",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
